#. The Activities screen: a screen's title, top left; about 96 pixels in the title font
msgctxt "hub.activities-title"
msgid "My Activities"
msgstr "Eigene Aktivitäten"

#. The Activities screen when there are none: a message centred on the screen; about 160 pixels a line
msgctxt "hub.no-activities"
msgid "No activities"
msgstr "Keine Aktivitäten"

#. The device list: a screen's title, top left; about 96 pixels in the title font
msgctxt "hub.devices-title"
msgid "Devices"
msgstr "Geräte"

#. The device list when there are none: a message centred on the screen; about 160 pixels a line
msgctxt "hub.no-devices"
msgid "No devices"
msgstr "Keine Geräte"

#. The key test screen: a screen's title, top left; about 96 pixels in the title font
msgctxt "keytest.title"
msgid "Key test"
msgstr "Tastentest"

#. The key test, before a key: a message centred on the screen; about 160 pixels a line
msgctxt "keytest.prompt"
msgid "Press any key"
msgstr "Drücken Sie eine Taste"

#. The key test: {code} is the code the key sent, e.g. C02B. a message centred on the screen; about 160 pixels a line
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "keytest.pressed"
msgid "That was {code}"
msgstr "Das war {code}"

#. The key test, after a key: a message centred on the screen; about 160 pixels a line
msgctxt "keytest.again"
msgid "Press another key"
msgstr "Drücken Sie eine weitere Taste"

#. The key test: how to leave it. a message centred on the screen; about 160 pixels a line
msgctxt "keytest.back"
msgid "Touch the screen to go back"
msgstr "Tippen Sie auf den Bildschirm, um zurückzukehren"

#. The light test screen: a screen's title, top left; about 96 pixels in the title font
msgctxt "lighttest.title"
msgid "Light test"
msgstr "Lichttest"

#. The light test: {led} is the LED's number, 0 to 6. a message centred on the screen; about 160 pixels a line
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "lighttest.lit"
msgid "Only LED {led} is lit"
msgstr "Nur LED {led} leuchtet"

#. The light test: how to go on. a message centred on the screen; about 160 pixels a line
msgctxt "lighttest.next"
msgid "Touch the screen for the next"
msgstr "Tippen Sie auf den Bildschirm für die nächste"

#. Opens Options: a softkey label, bottom of the screen; one line of about 116 pixels
msgctxt "softkey.options"
msgid "Options"
msgstr "Optionen"

#. Back to Activities: a softkey label, bottom of the screen; one line of about 116 pixels
msgctxt "softkey.activities"
msgid "Activities"
msgstr "Aktivitäten"

#. Opens the device list: a softkey label, bottom of the screen; one line of about 116 pixels
msgctxt "softkey.devices"
msgid "Devices"
msgstr "Geräte"

#. Back to the activity that is running, from the device list and a device's screens: a softkey label, bottom of the screen; one line of about 116 pixels
msgctxt "softkey.current-activity"
msgid "Current Activity"
msgstr "Aktuelle Aktivität"

#. After a screen's page total, e.g. '1/3 pages', in the small counter font; about 40 pixels
msgctxt "pages"
msgid "page"
msgid_plural "pages"
msgstr[0] "Seite"
msgstr[1] "Seiten"

#. While an activity starts, under its icon; {activity} is its name. Two lines at most, of about 164 pixels, then cut
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "activity.starting"
msgid "Starting {activity}"
msgstr "Start {activity}"

#. While an activity starts or Help is fixing it, at the bottom: a message centred on the screen; about 160 pixels a line; two lines at most
msgctxt "activity.keep-pointed"
msgid "Keep the remote pointed at your system."
msgstr "Zeigen Sie mit der Fernbedienung weiterhin auf die Anlage."

#. Help, under the activity's name, while it re-sends what the activity needs: a message centred on the screen; about 160 pixels a line
msgctxt "activity.fixing"
msgid "Attempting to fix the problem..."
msgstr "Es wird versucht, das Problem zu lösen..."

#. The title of Help when nothing is running, while it turns everything off again: a screen's title, top left; about 96 pixels in the title font
msgctxt "activity.power-off"
msgid "Power Off"
msgstr "Aus"

#. On an activity's commands, opens its number keypad: a softkey label, bottom of the screen; one line of about 116 pixels
msgctxt "softkey.numbers"
msgid "123"
msgstr "123"

#. On the number keypad, back to the activity's commands: a softkey label, bottom of the screen; one line of about 116 pixels
msgctxt "softkey.back"
msgid "Back"
msgstr "Zurück"

#. On an activity's favourite channels, opens its commands: a softkey label, bottom of the screen; one line of about 116 pixels
msgctxt "softkey.commands"
msgid "Commands"
msgstr "Befehle"

#. On an activity's commands, opens its favourite channels: a softkey label, bottom of the screen; one line of about 116 pixels
msgctxt "softkey.favourites"
msgid "Favorites"
msgstr "Favoriten"

#. Help, at the bottom while it re-sends: a message centred on the screen; about 160 pixels a line; two lines
msgctxt "help.keep-pointed"
msgid "Keep the remote pointed to your system."
msgstr "Zeigen Sie mit der Fernbedienung auf die Anlage."

#. Help's first question, after it has re-sent everything; a line break starts the explanation below it: a message centred on the screen; about 160 pixels a line
msgctxt "help.fixed-first"
msgid "Did that fix the problem?\nIf not, the remote will ask you questions to help correct the problem."
msgstr "Wurde das Problem gelöst?\nFalls nicht, stellt die Fernbedienung weitere Fragen, um das Problem zu beheben."

#. Help, after a device answered: a message centred on the screen; about 160 pixels a line
msgctxt "help.fixed"
msgid "Did that fix the problem?"
msgstr "Wurde das Problem gelöst?"

#. Help pressed with nothing on, when no device has a power to ask about; OK goes back: a message centred on the screen; about 160 pixels a line
msgctxt "help.nothing-to-do"
msgid "Nothing to do"
msgstr "Nichts zu tun"

#. Help asks about each device an activity turns on; {device} is its name: a message centred on the screen; about 160 pixels a line; three lines at most
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "assistant.is-on"
msgid "Is the {device} on?"
msgstr "Ist {device} eingeschaltet?"

#. Help asks again after sending its power: a message centred on the screen; about 160 pixels a line
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "assistant.now-on"
msgid "Now is the {device} on?"
msgstr "Ist {device} jetzt eingeschaltet?"

#. Help asks about each input; {device} and {input} are names: a message centred on the screen; about 160 pixels a line; three lines at most
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "assistant.input"
msgid "Is the {device} set to the {input} input?"
msgstr "Ist für {device} der Eingang {input} gewählt?"

#. Help asks again after sending the input: a message centred on the screen; about 160 pixels a line
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "assistant.now-input"
msgid "Now is the {device} set to the {input} input?"
msgstr "Ist für {device} jetzt der Eingang {input} gewählt?"

#. Help, for a device the remote has no power command for; OK goes on: a message centred on the screen; about 160 pixels a line
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "assistant.ensure-on"
msgid "Ensure the {device} is on."
msgstr "Stellen Sie sicher, dass {device} eingeschaltet ist."

#. Help, for an input no command selects; OK goes on: a message centred on the screen; about 160 pixels a line
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "assistant.ensure-input"
msgid "Ensure the {device} is set to the {input} input."
msgstr "Stellen Sie sicher, dass für {device} der Eingang {input} gewählt ist."

#. Off's Help asks about each device: a message centred on the screen; about 160 pixels a line
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "assistant.is-off"
msgid "Is the {device} off?"
msgstr "Ist {device} ausgeschaltet?"

#. Off's Help asks again after turning it off: a message centred on the screen; about 160 pixels a line
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "assistant.now-off"
msgid "Now is the {device} off?"
msgstr "Ist {device} jetzt ausgeschaltet?"

#. An answer, bottom left: a softkey label, bottom of the screen; one line of about 116 pixels
msgctxt "softkey.yes"
msgid "Yes"
msgstr "Ja"

#. An answer, bottom right: a softkey label, bottom of the screen; one line of about 116 pixels
msgctxt "softkey.no"
msgid "No"
msgstr "Nein"

#. Closes a Remote Assistant note, bottom right: a softkey label, bottom of the screen; one line of about 116 pixels
msgctxt "softkey.ok"
msgid "OK"
msgstr "OK"

#. The Remote Assistant's screens: the activity's name, or Off's, as their title: a screen's title, top left; about 96 pixels in the title font
#, python-brace-format
msgctxt "assistant.title"
msgid "{name}:"
msgstr "{name}:"

#. Above each Remote Assistant note: a message centred on the screen; about 160 pixels a line
msgctxt "assistant.heading"
msgid "Remote Assistant:"
msgstr "Fernbedienungs-Assistent:"

#. After an activity starts: a message centred on the screen; about 160 pixels a line
msgctxt "assistant.press-help"
msgid "If any devices are not set up correctly, press \"Help\" now."
msgstr "Falls Geräte nicht richtig eingestellt sind, drücken Sie jetzt die Taste Help."

#. After an activity starts, once Remote Assistant is back on: a message centred on the screen; about 160 pixels a line
msgctxt "assistant.set-up"
msgid "The remote has now set up your system for this Activity."
msgstr "Die Fernbedienung hat Ihre Anlage jetzt für diese Aktivität eingerichtet."

#. Above Yes and No: a message centred on the screen; about 160 pixels a line
msgctxt "assistant.hide"
msgid "Do you want to hide the Remote Assistant?"
msgstr "Möchten Sie den Fernbedienungs-Assistenten ausblenden?"

#. After choosing to hide it: a message centred on the screen; about 160 pixels a line
msgctxt "assistant.how-to-hide"
msgid "To hide the remote assistant, use the software to update the display settings for your remote."
msgstr "Um den Fernbedienungs-Assistenten auszublenden, ändern Sie mit der Software die Anzeigeeinstellungen Ihrer Fernbedienung."

#. The first note a new remote shows, when it starts: a message centred on the screen; about 160 pixels a line
msgctxt "assistant.welcome"
msgid "Welcome to your remote."
msgstr "Willkommen bei Ihrer Fernbedienung."

#. After Off: a message centred on the screen; about 160 pixels a line
msgctxt "assistant.all-off"
msgid "Ensure all your devices are off.  If any devices are still on, press \"Help\" now."
msgstr "Stellen Sie sicher, dass alle Geräte ausgeschaltet sind. Falls noch Geräte eingeschaltet sind, drücken Sie jetzt die Taste Help."

#. An Options row while the Remote Assistant asks after each start: a row label, centred on a 164-pixel row
msgctxt "options.assistant-off"
msgid "Turn Remote Assistant Off"
msgstr "Fernbedienungs-Assistent ausschalten"

#. An Options row while it does not: a row label, centred on a 164-pixel row
msgctxt "options.assistant-on"
msgid "Turn Remote Assistant On"
msgstr "Fernbedienungs-Assistent einschalten"

#. An Options row: a row label, centred on a 164-pixel row
msgctxt "options.tutorial"
msgid "Tutorial"
msgstr "Tutorial"

#. The Tutorial's screens: a screen's title, top left; about 96 pixels in the title font
msgctxt "tutorial.title"
msgid "Tutorial"
msgstr "Tutorial"

#. Leaves the Tutorial: a softkey label, bottom of the screen; one line of about 116 pixels
msgctxt "softkey.exit"
msgid "Exit"
msgstr "Beenden"

#. A Tutorial page, from the left, about 160 pixels a line; a line break starts a new paragraph. The last paragraph says which key moves on.
msgctxt "tutorial.1"
msgid "Welcome to your Harmony 800 touch-screen remote. Touch the screen to learn more."
msgstr "Willkommen bei Ihrer neuen Fernbedienung Harmony 800 mit Touchscreen. Tippen Sie auf den Bildschirm."

#. A Tutorial page, from the left, about 160 pixels a line; a line break starts a new paragraph. The last paragraph says which key moves on.
msgctxt "tutorial.2"
msgid "Use the arrow buttons on the sides of this screen to move between pages.\nPress the right arrow now."
msgstr "Mit den seitlichen Pfeiltasten blättern Sie zwischen den Seiten.\nDrücken Sie jetzt die rechte Pfeiltaste."

#. A Tutorial page, from the left, about 160 pixels a line; a line break starts a new paragraph. The last paragraph says which key moves on.
msgctxt "tutorial.3"
msgid "The Harmony remote uses Activities to give you simple one-touch control of your entertainment system.\nPress the Activities button now."
msgstr "Die Harmony-Fernbedienung verwendet Aktivitäten, über die Sie Ihre Home-Entertainment-Anlage mit nur einem Tastendruck steuern können.\nDrücken Sie die Taste Activities."

#. A Tutorial page, from the left, about 160 pixels a line; a line break starts a new paragraph. The last paragraph says which key moves on.
msgctxt "tutorial.4"
msgid "Activities are what you actually do with your entertainment system, like watch TV or listen to music.\nTouch Watch TV now."
msgstr "Als Aktivität wird alles bezeichnet, was Sie mit Ihrem Home-Entertainment-System tun können, z. B. fernsehen oder Musik hören.\nTippen Sie jetzt auf Fernsehen."

#. A Tutorial page, from the left, about 160 pixels a line; a line break starts a new paragraph. The last paragraph says which key moves on.
msgctxt "tutorial.5"
msgid "Selecting the Watch TV Activity turns on the devices you use to watch TV.\nPress the right arrow to continue."
msgstr "Wenn Sie die Aktivität Fernsehen wählen, werden alle Geräte eingeschaltet, die Sie zum Fernsehen benötigen.\nDrücken Sie die rechte Pfeiltaste."

#. A Tutorial page, from the left, about 160 pixels a line; a line break starts a new paragraph. The last paragraph says which key moves on.
msgctxt "tutorial.6"
msgid "Look on the screen for functions you can't find elsewhere on the remote.\nPress the right arrow to continue."
msgstr "Auf dem LCD finden Sie zusätzliche Funktionen, die sonst nicht auf Ihrer Fernbedienung enthalten sind.\nDrücken Sie die rechte Pfeiltaste."

#. A Tutorial page, from the left, about 160 pixels a line; a line break starts a new paragraph. The last paragraph says which key moves on.
msgctxt "tutorial.7"
msgid "To select another Activity, simply press the Activities button.\nPress the right arrow to continue."
msgstr "Zum Auswählen einer anderen Aktivität drücken Sie einfach erneut auf Activities.\nDrücken Sie die rechte Pfeiltaste."

#. A Tutorial page, from the left, about 160 pixels a line; a line break starts a new paragraph. The last paragraph says which key moves on.
msgctxt "tutorial.8"
msgid "Use the Help button if your Activity doesn't start properly.\nPress Help now."
msgstr "Drücken Sie die Taste Help, wenn die Aktivität nicht korrekt gestartet wird.\nDrücken Sie jetzt Help."

#. A Tutorial page, from the left, about 160 pixels a line; a line break starts a new paragraph. The last paragraph says which key moves on.
msgctxt "tutorial.9"
msgid "Help asks you questions to get your Activity back on track. Press the right arrow to continue."
msgstr "Wenn Sie die Taste Help drücken, werden Ihnen einfache Fragen gestellt, mit denen Sie das Problem lösen können. Drücken Sie die rechte Pfeiltaste."

#. A Tutorial page, from the left, about 160 pixels a line; a line break starts a new paragraph. The last paragraph says which key moves on.
msgctxt "tutorial.10"
msgid "To turn off your entertainment system, press the Power button.\nPress the Power button to continue."
msgstr "Zum Ausschalten Ihrer Home Entertainment-Anlage drücken Sie die Taste Power.\nDrücken Sie jetzt Power."

#. A Tutorial page, from the left, about 160 pixels a line; a line break starts a new paragraph. The last paragraph says which key moves on.
msgctxt "tutorial.11"
msgid "It's that easy!\nYou can now enjoy your entertainment system with one-touch Activity control.\nPress Exit now."
msgstr "So einfach ist das!\nMit nur einem Tastendruck können Sie jetzt alle Funktionen Ihrer Anlage steuern.\nDrücken Sie jetzt Beenden."

#. On the activity row the Tutorial pictures; about 100 pixels
msgctxt "tutorial.watch-tv"
msgid "Watch TV"
msgstr "Fernsehen"

#. On a button the Tutorial pictures: a button label, centred on a 81-pixel button; may wrap to two lines
msgctxt "tutorial.display"
msgid "Display"
msgstr "Display"

#. On a button the Tutorial pictures: a button label, centred on a 81-pixel button; may wrap to two lines
msgctxt "tutorial.aspect"
msgid "Aspect"
msgstr "Bildformat"

#. The question the Tutorial pictures Help asking: a message centred on the screen; about 160 pixels a line
msgctxt "tutorial.is-tv-on"
msgid "Is the TV on?"
msgstr "Ist der Fernseher eingeschaltet?"

#. On a button the Tutorial pictures: a button label, centred on a 81-pixel button; may wrap to two lines
msgctxt "tutorial.yes"
msgid "Yes"
msgstr "Ja"

#. On a button the Tutorial pictures: a button label, centred on a 81-pixel button; may wrap to two lines
msgctxt "tutorial.no"
msgid "No"
msgstr "Nein"

